    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Flocks streaming along each flyway (orange Arctic tern, \
Atlantic basin; cyan common swift, Afro-Palearctic; gold red knot, Americas). \
Birds are spaced along each species' resampled monthly path; this is a \
visualisation of the centroid route, not tracked individuals.\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic,
       FontColor->GrayLevel[0.35]],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->460]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Automatic, Automatic}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"aa37783e-96d8-473a-a192-97314e9c832d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The flock frames are generated by ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/flock.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", which jitters a small swarm around each species' resampled monthly \
centroid path and renders the orthographic globe frame by frame."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"96e8b575-45c1-4ca8-9371-a435bbe78ccf"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.  Speeds and stopovers", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"f70b448c-bc9a-4ae4-af6c-d64e48ff0d97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The basic question.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " If the centre of mass of a population moves across the planet over a year, \
",
 StyleBox["how fast does it move, and when does it pause?",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " A migration is not a steady glide: it is bursts of hard travel separated \
by long stationary spells on the breeding and wintering grounds. The monthly \
centroid track of \[Section]4 already contains that rhythm \[LongDash] we \
just have to differentiate it."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"992cf800-6ab6-4fd2-b47e-7c805f1955be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The quantity.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " For each species we take the great-circle distance between consecutive \
monthly centroids and divide by the number of days in the step, giving a ",
 StyleBox["centroid ground speed in km/day",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". Read off the per-flyway tracks, the means and peaks differ sharply: the \
Arctic tern's centre of mass averages about ",
 StyleBox["66 km/day",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " and peaks near ",
 StyleBox["135 km/day",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " during passage; the common swift averages about ",
 StyleBox["38 km/day",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " and the red knot about ",
 StyleBox["22 km/day",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"5f54dd9f-5187-4bb0-a396-5879dcf613b2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* Monthly centroid ground speed (km/day) from the per-flyway track.
   Abbreviated from wolfram/journey_metrics.wls. *)
days = {31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31};
step[c_] := MapThread[
   GeoDistance[GeoPosition[#1], GeoPosition[#2]] &,
   {Most[c], RotateLeft[c][[;; -2]]}];   (* consecutive monthly hops *)
speedKmDay[c_] := QuantityMagnitude[step[c], \"Kilometers\"] / Rest[days];
ListLinePlot[speedKmDay /@ {tern, swift, knot},
   PlotLegends -> {\"Arctic tern\", \"common swift\", \"red knot\"},
   AxesLabel -> {\"month\", \"km/day\"}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"746a082e-66ed-4ed6-a5a6-efc831a2d9a9"],

