Cell["\<\
Figure 8.2  Magnetic dip and total-field intensity sampled month by month \
along each species' centroid route \[LongDash] the magnetic \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]signature\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] a bird on that \
flyway would experience through the year.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"adf10e8d-892a-4190-a121-8a3a433053bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What this shows \[LongDash] and what it cannot. ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "All three tracks cross a wide span of magnetic dip \[LongDash] about ",
 StyleBox["132\[Degree]",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " for the Arctic tern, ",
 StyleBox["109\[Degree]",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " for the common swift, and ",
 StyleBox["36\[Degree]",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " for the red knot \[LongDash] so the field carries a strong, monotone \
latitude signal along each route. In fact, along these tracks inclination is \
almost perfectly a function of latitude (corr(dip, lat) \[TildeTilde] ",
 StyleBox["0.99",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "), exactly as the geocentric-dipole relation ",
 StyleBox["tan I = 2 tan \[Lambda]",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (with \[Lambda] the magnetic latitude) predicts; the longitude-only \
contribution to dip is tiny (\[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["2.7\[Degree]",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "). ",
 StyleBox["So the field does provide a usable latitude gauge in principle. \
But occurrence centroids cannot test whether the birds actually use it.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " We are showing the magnetic landscape these populations traverse, not a \
navigational mechanism: nothing here demonstrates that the birds read, \
follow, or steer by the field. That would require individual tracking, not \
where-the-crowd-is data."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {6, 10}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.6, 0.15],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1., 0.97, 0.88],ExpressionUUID->"36049257-e017-4566-bde7-5dc6c7726efe"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.  Cross-check: eBird Status & Trends", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"3b79641b-c2e4-460e-abb9-d0cc50147e91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Are our occurrence-based centroids actually right?",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " A method built from biased citizen-science occurrences deserves an \
independent check. Cornell's ",
 StyleBox["eBird Status & Trends",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (S&T) is the professional answer to the same question: it fits \
machine-learning models that explicitly correct for observer effort and \
detectability, and outputs ",
 StyleBox["bias-corrected weekly relative abundance",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " on a fine grid \[LongDash] a far more sophisticated product than our \
coarse occurrence centroid (Fink et al., eBird Status and Trends)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"5b9b0019-d8e3-4442-b45f-38afa6e00617"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As a ",
 StyleBox["private validation",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", we computed abundance-weighted centroids directly from the S&T rasters \
\[LongDash] inside the ",
 StyleBox["same",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " flyway boxes used in \[Section]4 \[LongDash] by driving the R ",
 StyleBox["ebirdst",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " package from Wolfram Language via ",
 StyleBox["ExternalEvaluate",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", then measuring the great-circle separation between Cornell's modelled \
centroids and ours, month by month. The pattern of code (our code, not \
Cornell's data) is:"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"7eff6adc-c11b-49fa-9516-c98f968acb6d"],

Cell["\<\
(* PRIVATE S&T validation: abundance-weighted centroids from the
   ebirdst weekly rasters, compared to our GBIF centroids in the same
   flyway box. The rasters and all derived S&T artifacts stay LOCAL and
   git-ignored, per Cornell's terms -- only this code is shared. *)
r = StartExternalSession[\"R\"];
ExternalEvaluate[r, \"library(ebirdst); library(terra)\"];
ExternalEvaluate[r, \"
  cube <- load_raster(species, product='abundance', period='weekly')
  ll   <- project(cube, '+proj=longlat')
\"];
(* For each of 52 weekly layers: abundance-weighted lon/lat centroid,
   cropped to the flyway box, then resampled WL-side to 12 monthly means
   and compared to the GBIF track with GeoDistance. *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"89b251a9-734d-4180-922d-4e37af4202c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The result.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " Our occurrence-based centroids agree with Cornell's professionally \
modelled abundance centroids to within roughly ",
 StyleBox["1,300\[Dash]1,750 km",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " on average, along flyways thousands of kilometres long: common swift ~",
 "1283",
 " km, red knot ~",
 "1392",
 " km, Arctic tern ~",
 "1742",
 " km mean monthly separation. For a coarse, presence-weighted method built \
from raw occurrence data, agreeing with a full effort-corrected model to \
within a small fraction of the flyway length is a strong endorsement that the \
centroid approach captures the real seasonal signal."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"2aab7879-c679-41cb-bb69-3bb2712faed4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why you see no S&T figure here.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " The eBird Status & Trends Data Products are released under Cornell's own \
terms, which permit ",
 StyleBox["non-commercial use and validation",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " but do ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " permit publishing derived figures or maps. We therefore show ",
 StyleBox["none",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] the cross-check above is reported as numbers only \[LongDash] \
and we point readers to Cornell's official, professionally produced \
visualizations instead: ",
 StyleBox["eBird Status and Trends",
  FontWeight->"SemiBold"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["https://science.ebird.org/en/status-and-trends",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->10],
 ")",
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"c8f8589d-5a47-4b88-9afc-1135bfbceb57"],

Cell["\<\
This material uses data from the eBird Status and Trends Project at the \
Cornell Lab of Ornithology, eBird.org. Any opinions, findings, and \
conclusions or recommendations expressed in this material are those of the \
author(s) and do not necessarily reflect the views of the Cornell Lab of \
Ornithology.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {10, 10}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.153, 0.51, 0.64],
 FontSize->12,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.95, 0.97],ExpressionUUID->"eb8c0fa6-3e95-4d15-9120-9dddfce0bd02"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9b.  Live now: recent sightings via the eBird API", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"eb64a95a-cb54-47b5-b831-1c0a13bff02a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The centroids summarise a decade of history. For a sense of where these \
birds are ",
 StyleBox["this month",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", we add a live layer pulled from the ",
 StyleBox["eBird API 2.0",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " recent-observations endpoint (",
 StyleBox["/v2/data/obs/{region}/recent/{speciesCode}",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "), which returns the last 30 days of checklisted sightings for a species in \
a region. We sweep a representative spread of countries and plot the result:"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"1c7b966c-3b95-4a94-94fe-53c0d0a3d4a4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* Live recent sightings (last 30 days, as of late June 2026). \
LoadLiveSightings sweeps a
   spread of regions, returns {lat,lon} pairs ROUNDED TO 0.1 deg for
   privacy. Supply your own eBird API 2.0 token. *)
pts = LoadLiveSightings[\"arcter\", \"<your-ebird-api-token>\"];  (* \
arcter|comswi|redkno *)
GeoListPlot[GeoPosition /@ pts, GeoRange -> \"World\",
   GeoProjection -> \"Robinson\", GeoBackground -> GrayLevel[0.15],
   PlotStyle -> Directive[Orange, Opacity[0.7], PointSize[0.006]],
   PlotLabel -> \"Arctic tern -- recent eBird sightings (last 30 d)\\n\\
Source: eBird.org (Cornell Lab of Ornithology)\", ImageSize -> 900]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"cd338a7c-8d19-4b01-9197-f28e0069ace7"],

